  "_what_this_is": "The projects a resident of this service area is most likely to search for. Trackstar is not judged on how many records it holds; it is judged on whether the project someone actually asked about is right. This file is that list, and the state of each entry was measured against the live API, not asserted.",
  "_how_to_read_it": "tier 'guaranteed' means the project is found and placed today and a regression that loses it is a failure. tier 'found_unmapped' means Trackstar knows the project exists but cannot defensibly place it, which is a real gap a resident would notice on the map. tier 'watchlist' means the project is high-interest and Trackstar cannot find it at all - it is a target, and it must not be allowed to fail a build, because a gate that is always red is a gate nobody reads.",
  "_selection": "There is no government ranking of 'top projects' and no Trackstar search log yet, so this set is an editorial judgement from project scale, construction impact, recency, controversy and how likely a normal person is to recognise the name. It is a target set, not a measured search ranking, and it should be replaced by real query logs the moment there are any.",
